hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1067","Chapter on emigration, 1105 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi narrated to me, he said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about emigration. He said: Woe to you, emigration is a grave matter. Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: Do you pay their charity? He said: Yes. He said: Do you grant some of them for use? He said: Yes. He said: Do you milk them for others on the day they are brought to water? He said: Yes. He said: Then work beyond the seas, for Allah will not diminish anything of your deeds."
"1068","1106 - Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no emigration after the Conquest, and when you are called to march forth, then march forth."
